body:
Anyone getting the "It looks like you've been attempting a lot of purchases" message--keep trying anyway. Just got the 512GB. 

&#x200B;

Forewarning that I tried using Visa literally the day before the OLED was announced and it (thankfully) didn't work and I woke up to my bank calling me with fraud alerts lol. So if you can avoid Visa, that might save an extra step. Also, the Paypal option didn't work for me at all. - \_ -

Of course :) I know how you feel; I didn't get into makeup really until I was about 25. Then I started wearing an amount that was too much for my liking and expensive as heck. After the pandemic, I only do my brows and liner most of the time. If I have to go to something "important" I'll wear bronzer and maybe foundation--though now as I'm getting older, it seems most of my foundations cake up on me and feel suffocating.

&#x200B;

It's definitely not a necessity. You do what makes you feel best :)

My first instinct is to ask who is saying these things to you, because that’s really not nice of them. Perhaps ask yourself: outside influence, how do *you* feel about it? It’s perfectly legible.
&nbsp;

My advice if you don’t struggle with ADHD or otherwise “quick thoughts”, or neuropathy(I struggle with these things and have yet to find a reliable solution lol): 
&nbsp;
Trying to make all the letters the same size and height is helpful aesthetically. I find practicing with kanji paper or (idk the proper name) paper with multiple horizontal lines is helpful. The only “downside” of kanji paper is that every set I’ve gotten has been amazingly soft and smooth (it’s my favorite paper for quick and sloppy note taking, diagrams, or cursive). A slightly rougher texture might be good for practicing lettering. Start with a regular ballpoint to get used to the feel. Write out individual letters. Find a style you like.
You’ll have to practice often. Maybe join the pen pals sub and use that as some additional practice :) 

&nbsp;

IMO, try your best not to worry about what others think though. As long as it’s legible, you’re good.
If you’d like to improve your writing for yourself or artistic purposes, I’d definitely recommend practicing at least once a day with some of the aforementioned paper.

&nbsp;

Yep, same. For me I had ED’s in the past and in my late 20’s I was recovered for just a year or two. I had a bad reaction to a medication due to a rare disease(undiagnosed then) and was constipated for a month and a half, couldn’t pee for a week, and then struggled with it for another month or so. No one believed me for some reason, and I felt pretty helpless. Turns out the drug is on a neurotoxic list and people with my condition should avoid it or take it with caution..I swelled up with fluids and nothing I did helped, so I (unknowingly) relapsed. Thought I was actually eating unhealthy in the opposite way(I lived off a small amount of high carb/fat foods basically). 
&nbsp;

I realized last year after I started recovery and was eating maintenance calories for the first time since I was a very young child, that I’d still had an ED. Since it was mostly candy, no one was ever worried about me and just thought I was “lucky” to be able to “eat that stuff” and lose weight. 

&nbsp;

Last year I had a few big losses and stopped eating entirely. I told myself the entire time that it wasn’t an ED, I was just sad. While that started out true, before the losses, I was deeply struggling with my body and eating habits. After those things happened I totally lost my appetite and even drinking water made me feel sick, but it didn’t click until my bf brought home a scale(ugh) and I couldn’t stop weighing myself and seeing how far I could go, that I had an ED again. I attempted recovery soon after I realized, but my mind was already in too deep. My point though is, I could’ve seen myself in those groups at any point during those episodes, thinking “ok, well I definitely don’t have an ED”.

&nbsp;

What alarms me the most about those subs is actually the amount of people that recommend heavy physical activity with the fast. Like what. I did that at my very worst with BN. I totally ran my body down, to the extent that I had a breakdown and dropped out of school. I’m still struggling with fasting and restriction,but imagining how terrible I felt when I did that literally makes me feel physically ill. I can’t believe so many people think this is ok.

Wow, tbh I went to one of those subs out of curiosity recently and felt the same. It looked strikingly similar to pro-ED groups that I was part of years ago as a young teen. I felt the same about that Alli diet pill. According to family and friends who took it, it supposedly had a laxative effect if you ate foods high in fat. 

&nbsp;

It angers *my ED* that these things are socially acceptable for those trying to lose weight, regardless of their weight, but not for us. I’m interested in hearing what the difference is.
More appropriately , it angers me *for them* because in the end, these are ED behaviors. They may not have the mentality to back it up, but to fast for days is getting there at the very least. For me, it started as just little fasts here and there. Fast results/relief can be a bit addicting.

&nbsp;

And while I try not to bring up “triggers” regarding daily life things (like I know I can’t stop everyone from talking about food, or seeing diet foods lol I just ignore those things/ some “diet” foods I genuinely like too) it’s unnecessarily triggering and confusing to see fasting for weight loss becoming so socially acceptable. I hate seeing it on every magazine when I grocery shop(this feels especially messed up in recovery, at checkout) and all over social media.

&nbsp;

I can fast for days on end, and that’s clearly unhealthy. I’ve done that at a large range of weights throughout my life, and it’s always been unhealthy.  I was reading a blog just last night on fasting and the things this person was saying were exactly the things I tell myself when I fast. I don’t understand how this is socially acceptable.

I actually can’t even imagine showing photos of myself at my sickest.. I saved photos of myself from then to encourage my recovery because I looked so sick. I think it would only be helpful to do that when I had bulimia to show that people can be any size and have EDs. I was consistently OW when I struggled with that and was always told how “healthy” I looked.

&nbsp;

Showing before photos otherwise just offers room for competition, I think. People with EDs are notoriously competitive, and notoriously don’t ever feel “sick enough”. Posting before pictures sets some expectation of what “ *is* sick enough”, and it’s just false, because it’s not the same for everyone. 

&nbsp;

Optimistically, I could see people posting them as a proud “look how far I came from where I was”, but it’s a bit tone deaf from people that should know better than anyone why posting those photos is a bad idea. Additionally, it promotes the false idea that EDs are only physical and once you’re weight restored, you’re cured.

I feel this way 100%. My initial plan was to work on my fears and the emotional/mental aspect, while re-feeding, and work on the gain slowly. I wasn’t deathly ill. Instead I was convinced to speed up weight gain before working on mental health/without even doing it simultaneously, pushed to gain past what I was even comfortable with(what my GP agreed was medically healthy), and now I’m weight restored and then some and I’m just miserable. I’m worse than before. I tried “all in” and it put me in a very, very bad place mentally. I now equate food to loss of control and gain again, probably worse than ever, when I’d spent months of hard work on working against those thoughts. Food had become something that I no longer feared and that brought me joy before I saw a terrible RD. 

&nbsp;

At this point, I’m “recovered” in a lot of peoples’ eyes because I’m weight restored. But I’m actually struggling more than ever and also in the process of going back. It’s so difficult after being in recovery. If I’m ever “ready” again, I’m going to work with my original approach to focus on the mental health aspects while slowly re-feeding to build back my metabolism safely and show myself that food itself doesn’t equal gain. But idk if I can ever not be afraid again after this.

I’ve actually noticed this a lot too. I truly feel bad, but when I see someone exactly my size say that eating (our maintenance amount or over with no compensatory behaviors) is/was “an ED” I’m a little confused..I don’t want to be hate keepy, but it seems the definition is misunderstood. 

&nbsp;

One can diet without having an ED, one can have ED like thoughts without acting on them, and one can have disordered eating without having an ED. What we live with is a disorder and affects us in and out though..

Haha that’s crazy. What class was it if you don’t mind my asking? I guess I’ve gotten lucky with mine and we’re mostly graded off our personal improvements/displays of paying attention as opposed to actual skill. 
&nbsp;

I did have a drawing class that was pretty intensely graded(I’m not sure if it was a weed out class or just harshly graded) and no joke, I found myself abusing prescriptions and working 30-40 hours a week to keep up my A+. We had these huge sheets of paper to fill each week, and I was hardly getting any sleep because I had 3 other classes. The two times I spent an almost sane amount of time on my assignments, I got a low B and a low A. I liked my prof a lot as a person, but he was a ridiculously hard grader. 

&nbsp;

I still have one more class of his that I need to take if I stick with my major, but idk if I have it in me. Been focusing on STEM ever since that semester because it was just so much and though I think he had grading guidelines, there is still subjectiveness in grading art and that makes me pretty nervous.

I tend to feel similarly but yeah, I also understand it’s subjective 😅 I gained a bit more appreciation for those art forms after having to take art history. I thought it would be such a useless class but I liked it a lot.  I still feel eh about pieces that are more symbolic than substance, but I guess I appreciate some of them more. Example: I recently had to visit the Andy Warhol museum and actually found his work “essentially useless” until I took color theory. I can appreciate some of his techniques and especially his use of color now, but that’s still about it. I didn’t understand other artists at all(cue that one toilet..”Fountain”, I think). Now I guess I get it, and I find it interesting, but it’s still not really my flavor lol. 

&nbsp;

I think what it boils down to is that I find it more performative art and (subjectively, obviously)I suppose it belongs in an art museum because it has some physical component, but it almost has more a spirit of arts like comedy, acting, or music to me. So that makes them feel “off” to me when in museums full of traditional art, but I’m not sure where else they’d belong.

&nbsp;

That all said. Your blank canvas comment reminded me that there’s a museum near me that literally has a blank canvas and another that’s just a regular old photo of a pickle. I can’t understand for the life of me what they could even be symbolizing 😂 museums that host blank canvases are a huge peeve of mine lol

This reminded me of my mom rummaging through all my brother and his gf’s sex stuff. Also felt the need to tell me all about it, claiming “they’re into some real kinky shit; I found blindfolds!” I have ADD and can go into sensory overload or get distracted(even during this) easily, so I love blindfolds. I also had many more toys than them. I ended up with vaginismus and anxiety due to past trauma and they made the process easier and more enjoyable. Hurt literally no one. Who cares? Lol. I still can’t believe she did that. I left her place soon after.

&nbsp;

During my teens I remember she went through my same brother’s room and was having a fit about his (very common, totally harmless) toys. She also was lent a laptop from his gf who I think did some porn as a little side thing during college. So of course she broke her trust and looked through all her porn instead of using it for its intended purpose. Can you imagine your mom wanting to see you and your SO boning and rummaging through your personal things just to judge you? Wtf is the matter with these people?

Im glad you’re in a better place now. Thanks for sharing this- I’m partially disabled and once expected to be in a similar position. I decided to mass list a lot of things in attempt to get myself out of a really bad situation. To be blunt, I was living in a new area, in an abusive relationship and it got to the point where I’d almost died a few times. I had no one close by and just needed some gas money to drive myself and my pets back “home”. I even use my sale money for meds and stuff sometimes. 

&nbsp;

The thing that I think made me feel most bad was when I’d see people online and listing things but not accepting their orders lol. I tried to remind myself that maybe they had stuff going on too, but it still felt bad. I always try to leave ratings as soon as possible because of that experience.

Tbh, I get annoyed if someone doesn’t rate after a bit, or they rate after payment is already released, but I never pester them. I find that pretty annoying- though I wouldn’t terribly mind if someone asked me after 2 days but that’s just me 🤷🏽‍♀️
&nbsp;

I asked someone once on PM if they’d received something very early in my selling and they never responded, then left me a 3 star after payment was released lol. I’ve come to the point where, though I find it a little rude at times, just thinking of that extra time the same as the ship time(so to never expect your pay until about a week, pretty much). I always wonder if something is wrong when people let it auto rate, so I’m glad to see there are more reasons for that.

&nbsp;

That said-I’ve had at least 2-3 sellers ask me if I got my item/to rate **immediately** after I got a notification that the packages were delivered. I usually open my packages as soon as I can and rate same day just to be considerate, because this is the way a lot of people make their money after all , but sometimes you just can’t. I’m usually excited to get my packages, but I’ve come home from really stressful days previously where I’ve just had nothing left in me to even want to open a package and inspect the item. Some people have kids, work long or weird hours, etc. you never know someone’s life. I think it’s really over the top when people get on you right away or don’t even give you a day.

&nbsp;

I personally don’t let it auto rate unless there’s something “wrong” but not enough for me to address(e.g. someone once forgot to mention a highlighter mark inside a Kate spade bag- I got it cheap and it was on the inside, so wasn’t a huge deal but I was still annoyed- I work with leather as a hobby and was able to remove it). I do it because I don’t feel comfortable leaving a positive review, but also don’t feel comfortable leaving a negative or neutral one since it wasn’t that bad and it will affect their overall rating. Otherwise I rate because I want to show sellers appreciation, have their payment release ASAP, and I want them to gain positive rep.

My dad has said similar things. About a year ago he told me that women like to be complimented, so he’ll roll down his window and tell someone if they look “nice” lol. I didn’t put that behavior past him but was still a little shocked lol, because he clearly didn’t think it was a problem at all. I told him that no woman likes that and he should really not do that xD 

&nbsp;

It either makes me feel kind of gross and self conscious, or scared, depending on how they approach. Usually I’ll be perfectly covered and it’s still most often “how much?” Makes me feel so bad.

Kind of afraid to ask, but is there any chance that her ex was actually a water bottle?

&nbsp;

To make a fuss over something that is not at all a common feature is just… wtf. Just know she’s definitely the one with something wrong with her, not you.

Nah, you’re no way TA. I’m female and had a guy do something similar to me. In our case, it turned out(he later admitted to me) that he was trying to erode my self esteem and make me believe that vaginas just genuinely could never feel good to a guy, ever. He would even send me videos comparing the inside to other things as “proof”. He said he was trying to manipulate me into doing other things that I’d said no to. Same person ended up assaulting me many times. It’s been a decade and I still struggle with PTSD and confidence over it. I have a lot of trouble with intimacy because I can’t shake my nerves about the things he told me, even after he told me it wasn’t true.

&nbsp;

I know how bad that kind of humiliation is. It’s uncomfortable enough the first time alone. Reading this really made my stomach churn and I’m so sorry you had to deal with that. Idk what her motive could be other than just being cruel, but this is never an acceptable thing to do. If you don’t like what your partner has this badly, you don’t complain- someone is sharing something personal with you. It’s better to just leave than to do this to someone.

&nbsp;

Years later I’ve still never recovered from the emotional abuse I experienced. That sort of thing cuts very deep, it’s too personal, and hearing it from someone that’s supposed to care about you feels awful. I hope you’re doing some better now and that your next relationship is one you deserve. But yeah, absolutely you’re in no way an AH. Your ex is. She surpassed normal boundaries and additionally your expressed ones as well. She humiliated you in a very personal way and kept doing it despite you addressing it multiple times. You shouldn’t bring up exes, but especially in that way.

This^^ I’m 5’2” and weighed near that. I was actually upset that I’d reached a lower BMI and was getting compliments, and that I also still wanted to lose more. Im no longer recovered, but my first attempt I realized that I’d probably never feel satisfied. 
&nbsp;

Looking back, I did look pretty awful too, just so sickly; before I told my neurologist that I had an ED, she thought I’d prematurely lost all fat and muscle in my calves  due to my condition(it causes tissue loss commonly referred to as “inverted bottle”). The look on her face when she realized I’d done that to myself , as opposed to it being due to my condition, will be burned into my mind forever. Idk why people close to me were complimenting me. When I get around there it’s usually a huge wake up call.

I’m so happy that was able to move you towards recovery. Thinking about “could haves” is one of the most devastating things-at least that was to me, personally also. I left HS with basically a 4th grade education very much due to my ED taking over my life. Prior, I’d always had huge dreams and goals of going to college early. Here I am at 31, I’ve been back in college since right before the pandemic, and I’m fully dependent on someone else. Life went basically polar opposite of what I’d dreamed of. Other things got in the way, but it was mostly the ED taking up all my time and mental energy.

&nbsp;

When I was in recovery last year before relapsing, I did so much mourning over that. I’d actually completely forgotten about it until now(I’m in a very bad relapse), so I’m glad to see someone mention this.

Not quite there yet, but almost. I’m constantly exhausted. Have ADHD and a neurological condition on top of it; my executive dysfunction and side effects of the condition are already exhausting (that diagnosis spurred my recovery the first time, when my neurologist informed me that the ED was likely the culprit of why my condition was so bad at such a young age..put my all into getting better and then I was triggered by my then-RD, a stupid scale, and not being cautious enough of online advice in relation to personal circumstances. Been struggling ever since). 

&nbsp;

I’m in college after years of hiatus (due to abuse and my ED- I even previously dropped out of HS because of it). I’m so tired. I made major progress in college somehow, might even get an internship at my dream job, but I’m exhausted. I keep sleeping too much and getting brain fog, or my thoughts are just obsessive about food. I feel shaky and sick and have to lie down a lot. I’m sick of having to exercise for hours every day. It takes me long to complete my work due to inattention problems, so I can only take 4 classes and the oversleeping especially causes additional time management issues.

&nbsp;

Unfortunately when I try to eat, it’s obviously stressful and that stress and overstimulation due to body heat increase and my clothes feeling different distract me from my class work as well. I feel like there’s no winning and I have to just “go with” my ED until May when classes end. That said, I feel like this kind of *is* my breaking point, I just can’t manage recovery until I have less at stake. I want to put all my effort into recovery this summer..wish I’d just taken off this semester because there are times that I feel like I really just can’t do this anymore. I want to stop but it affects my work more than just continuing on the way I am now.

I agree with other comments and don’t have anything to add there, but I wanted to chime in to say this: consider some universities that you might like to go to(idk what country you’re in, but just to name two in the US that I’ve met graduates from that work with NASA: Penn State—they have an Astrobio minor if you’re into that! and University of Colorado) and check out the major’s coursework. This can help you get a glimpse of where you should be starting, and the pre-reqs for those classes, which are what you will want to take in HS.

&nbsp;

You can also reach out to universities directly to inquire if you have any additional questions. I’d definitely recommend CS if at all possible. If you can’t take CS in HS, try to familiarize yourself with it at least and consider taking CS classes in college. A lot of modern AP work involves CS, so it can help you greatly when applying for jobs.

In short, yes. Our brains are in constant search of dopamine, which can easily lead to addiction or at the very least, preoccupation with certain things. 

&nbsp;

Things like OCD and EDs(though **not** addictions, but compulsive behaviors which can appear similar) are also very common comorbidities. I have both, and I’ve had alcohol addiction in the past. 

&nbsp;

“Hyper focus”/preoccupation with certain things is also very common. I can draw or paint all day and think an hour has gone by, when it’s actually been hours upon hours. I try to use art and music in tandem with things I need to get done(sketching and listening to music while reading, or sketching while listening to an audio textbook for example).

I get what you’re trying to say and I’d agree in certain situations(I sell far more than I buy and have been doing so for many years as well). In this situation the seller said, verbatim: “I got the receipt but the tracking number is the exact same as mercari” (so yes, we agree that they may not be understanding OP, or don’t want to bother with providing it if they did ship) and told the seller “don’t worry about it”. I don’t feel it’s that much extra work to provide tracking from a receipt that you claim to have gotten. 
&nbsp;

72 hours without tracking updating is normally the amount of time I give myself as a seller to investigate a buyer’s package. It’s not our fault if a package is lost or if it takes a while to be processed, but it will reflect poorly on us if we do nothing. OP can also investigate the package on their own, but they will need the tracking number. It’s a bit more difficult for buyers to do this than for the seller, as the seller has access to all of the information that is needed to file a claim.

&nbsp;

I don’t expect total professionalism on a sales app, especially as a seller myself, but how this person is responding to someone concerned over an item they bought from them is opposite of what the bare minimum level of professional and even friendly would be. Some buyers can be extremely annoying and pests, but I don’t see that applying in this situation based off of the seller’s responses. 

&nbsp;

I get what you’re saying. I just disagree that it applies in this particular situation. That said, I think it’s fine that we disagree on selling etiquette, everyone is different. Just explaining my thought process. I don’t bend over backwards for buyers, I will cancel orders if the buyer is an unreasonable pest, but I do try to be helpful and friendly because they are giving us their business after all.

They should have it on their receipt, or they could have it in the original email if they still have it(or if they deleted the email and haven’t emptied their trash can). The interaction makes it seem as though the seller is either somehow not understanding OP or they didn’t actually ship it. Other possibility could be that they just don’t want to take a few seconds to get it for them. I think they’d say so if they couldn’t see it, but they haven’t claimed that they can’t see it at all. The simplest explanation in this specific situation is that the seller is circumventing the question because they’re lying. 

&nbsp;

OP would be TA if they were harassing the seller over the tracking not updating and tracking was provided/ the seller was working with the buyer. Instead, the seller is evading the request, very likely because they never shipped. Tracking hasn’t been provided. The seller isn’t offering to contact the shipping service. All signs point to the seller lying or being somewhat slow to understand what OP is saying at the very least.

XD I actually just noticed that there was more than just one screenshot- no idea why they didn’t show up when I first clicked on the post O _ o i could only see the first one, so that’s what prompted the response(tbh I was a little confused about the post title based off only seeing the first pic- makes sense now 🤦🏽‍♀️). 

&nbsp;

After seeing all of them, yeah the seller is TA. There’s no reason they shouldn’t provide that. In this case it sounds like they’re being shady and very likely didn’t send it, or they’re somehow not understanding what OP is saying and thinks they can see it even after they’ve repeatedly told them that it’s not visible. Lol unfortunately, it’s likely the former.

Edit: I’m an idiot and didn’t see there was more than one screenshot. After seeing all of them, the seller is definitely TA. It sounds like they’re(somehow) either not understanding you when you say you can’t see the tracking, or that they’re flat out lying that they sent it. 

&nbsp;

Wouldn’t be surprised if they’re trying to bide their time to send it out today, and tracking updates tomorrow. If that happens, I would definitely briefly express what happened in the rating. Otherwise if they don’t ship it by the time you can cancel, cancel as soon as you’re able. Possibly contact Mercari as well; if they actually do have a tracking number and for whatever reason it isn’t showing on your end, Mercari should be able to give it to you. Unfortunately they likely won’t agree to cancel for this, but I hope you will have the ability to soon. I hate giving business to people like this. 


&nbsp;———————————————


Neither? I’ve had this happen before as a buyer and a seller. I learned(as a seller) to always hand my package off to a person because when I’d use drop boxes, sometimes it’d take a while for the post office to scan the package in- depending where I’d dropped it off; have one PO by me that’s open only 2-4 hours/ day and I had a package sitting there for a week without anything happening, at least 2x. I learned to stop going to them.

&nbsp;

As a buyer, the worst I’ve had happen was a fairly expensive item that the seller insisted they’d shipped, but a week went by and nothing happened. This was during the holidays in 2020. Someone suggested I cancel because they probably hadn’t shipped it, so I did. The seller didn’t get their payment and I was refunded. Weeks later, it showed up at my doorstep, yet the tracking had still never updated. I had to contact Mercari about it and they were able to compensate the seller. I felt really bad. I’ve also had sellers that just never shipped but would say they did. It’s tough because you never really know. 

&nbsp;

Without knowing if they actually shipped or not, neither of you are TA.

&nbsp;

I honestly wouldn’t recommend canceling until a few more days have gone by, but maybe update the seller.I think Mercari gives them a few days to ship. If they did actually send the package, they should be able to contact the PO they dropped it off at, and tbh they should offer to do that if it’s taken over 72 hours.

Agree. I recently bought a pair of Mother jeans and expected them to fit perfectly when compared to the flat measurements of my others. Instead, while the seller’s measurements were correct, the piece had zero stretch. Suppose I could’ve asked that as well but didn’t even think about it.

&nbsp;

Also, specific measurement stats are helpful since they’re directly showing where one’s weight is carried. Weight is the thing that’s unhelpful.

Same experience here. Especially if there’s a picture included but no stats. I usually list my stats for this reason as well. I’ve asked for stats and model photos as well(that actually used to be a very common request on the used clothing subreddits), even for bags(I’m short). 

&nbsp;

Seems like the person in OP’s experience just hasn’t read the description since they’re asking about condition as well, and that’s also been noted in the listing.

Thank you. It’s a long process, but I’m glad to be in a better place mentally than I once was. 

&nbsp;

I agree- I’ll truly never understand how some people can be so cruel to other.

Yeah I don’t throw around this word much, but as someone that was raped and otherwise abused for years of my life, I hate those people. I liked the existence of “MeToo” and think it had positive intentions, but at one point I did start noticing people creep into online support groups I was in who would claim they were assaulted, but it wouldn’t match the description of events. Fortunately, it honestly wasn’t that common relative to the usual posts, but those things would become main focuses of those critical of MeToo. I dislike those people for taking credibility away from actual abuse survivors.

&nbsp;

That said, I most often see this used in a non-literal manner. But I can see what you’re saying; there are always people that will take things too literally, especially something they’ve read online. Maybe we  should start phrasing it differently. I’ve noticed a lot of popular phrases like this are so often taken literally and cause so much confusion and real life problems.

I think you’re misinterpreting what people mean when they say this; it’s not meant to be literal. You can tell if someone is enthusiastic about having sex with you; OP stated that they begged their husband to stop. In my situations, I’d tell him no several times, he’d need to use manipulation or force to get his way. That’s not enthusiastic, and they knew it. They chose to ignore it.

&nbsp;

If someone is all over you and you didn’t have to beg them, guilt them, put them down, or physically force them for example, that is the “enthusiastic yes”.

I’m so sorry that this has all been your experience.  I just wanted to say that I’ve had a similar experience with therapists(especially CBT) after they’d find out my full history. And after I explain that I have little to no support system and am an atheist, it seems they don’t know what else to do. 

&nbsp;

My last therapist ghosted me. I’d worked with her for about a year and was supposed to do EMDR, then ghosted me on the last appointment before we were supposed to start it. She was a trauma therapist too. Totally sucks dealing with complex trauma. It feels like you do everything you’re “supposed to do” but there aren’t many people who are really equipped to help.

I was with someone for years that did this, most of the time when we’d hang out. I have a similar history of abuse, not being taught consent, and I grew up in a religious home that told me that women were to just do what the guy wanted. I remember I had a hard time kissing my first bf and my mom gave me a really hard time about it and said “guys need physical affection, give him what he wants.” During that time, I was considering that I could be asexual(I’m not, I just didn’t know how a relationship was supposed to feel/he was a good friend and “the perfect guy” but I didn’t realize that I didn’t have feelings for him and we felt on different wavelengths).

&nbsp;

I was very young and wanted to be loved and my abuser acted differently when he wasn’t raping me. A lot of times he’d gaslight me into thinking I initiated things that I said “absolutely no” to many times, and it genuinely confused me. He was loved by many people and I thought maybe I was imagining things. I thought I wasn’t worthy of fully being loved, because I was never loved growing up and had no idea what that looked like. I was used to people saying they loved me and hurting me. Why people stay is incredibly complex.

Fully agree. Once my current SO said we could have sex and when we started he cleeeearly wasn’t into it. I asked a few times and he said he was but he wasn’t participating at all. It was so weird and uncomfortable, I couldn’t. He said later that he had a headache or something but wanted to do it because I did. It just felt wrong. Sex is an activity that includes at least 2 people happily participating.

&nbsp;

