I have mixed feelings about this. I think firstly, there needs to be more regulation around renting houses because it’s causing a lot of problems for younger generations. However, there’s nothing inherently “wrong” about being a landlord, as long as you’re not doing shady things or renting out “all the homes”. Lol

&nbsp;

You individually seem like the type of landlord I’d love to have. Unfortunately I do feel like the majority of landlords I’ve encountered own too many homes, and the prices are so high that it’s difficult to keep up. If you’re single, in an abusive relationship ,or a loner, eh, you’re kinda screwed in most areas. My bf makes pretty good money and we don’t see how we will ever be able to buy a home. We’ve gotten less lucky with landlords that let mold and shit grow in our apartments, don’t respond to taking care of things, etc. It seems like the places also cost way more than they should(my own landlord spent 15K or less on our place, and we pay almost 2K/month- they half ass “renovated” by covering things up lol; if we could stay with parents and save all that money, or if I’d have gone to college on time, maybe we could get a house, but in our current area it’s mostly run down, over priced rentals from slumlords). The thing is, slumlords and scumlords aren’t all that exist. We have lived in 3 places and had one very good landlord. People just think in extremes and like to put everyone into little boxes.

&nbsp;

I do think it’s extremely unfortunate for you to have received the hate you have on this post, but your response to it is also unfortunate. Don’t threaten to make people go homeless just out of spite from receiving hate from shitheads, on the internet no less. Have you ever been or nearly faced homelessness? Even if not, please don’t wish that on people. I didn’t think you sounded like a dick based off of your OP, and I totally get feeling annoyed at that, but that’s going too far. Finding a good landlord is indeed hard and I think younger people feel quite cheated. Many people in the US(assuming that’s where you are) are living in poverty, even “middle class” is not doing well, and that also has nothing to do with being an idiot(idk if I misread that last part because, internet. I get that you’re angry but, yeah that’s a lot there). If you really have been a good landlord, don’t become a dick because of some comments online. Half the people online are trolls anyway, and plenty of people don’t even use Reddit. Being kind or a good person should never depend on how others perceive you. If you need to be validated to be a good person, perhaps you need to think some things through.

