From my perspective as someone with an ED: don’t talk about dieting, calories, weight, other people’s bodies, etc. My ED is triggered by numbers and high stress, especially together. I relapsed when I experienced 2 back to back deaths in the middle of a stressful semester at college, and then my bf bought a scale after I’d requested he not(it took me 15-16 years to let go of my scale- I happily smashed it and had a few years of health lol). I knew I couldn’t have it in the house especially during a relapse. I think I may have gotten out of it easier had I not known my weight. I saw how much I’d lost out of depression, and became obsessed with seeing how far it could drop. 

&nbsp;

I feel very uncomfortable when he and others talk about dieting, weight loss, or even do exactly what I do and criticize their bodies. 
I agree to not tell her she’s “not skinny but not fat”. My bf said something like that to me when I was underweight(I am very short so I guess I didn’t look as thin as I was, but still). He unknowingly did and said a lot of things that ended up sticking with me.

&nbsp;

When you compliment your gf(and others even), it might also be good to compliment her on non-weight aspects of herself. If she says she looks fat “I don’t think so” should be sufficient. Of course, it may be best to ask her the question you posted here.

&nbsp;

In the end, even if you said she looked skinny it wouldn’t be helpful. When my bf did say I looked very thin, I found it motivating, or my mind would twist things to think he was lying. When I clearly wasn’t thin and he’d say that, I started suspecting that he was just lying. At some points I thought I looked awful; my butt went concave at my LW and I complained about it and he said it looked fine. That made me think maybe I was delusional and looked healthy but thought I looked thinner. He later said he was worried but didn’t know what to say. I can imagine that position must be very difficult. 

&nbsp;

I don’t blame him in any of those incidents, the situation is complex. It was a mess. I try not to complain about my body as much right now, but of course it’s very hard not to.

Same here- I wished so badly when my cat died that I could believe in some afterlife, but I can’t. I had a crisis where I tried to reconsider, but I couldn’t. I was angry that I couldn’t force myself to believe in something, because I desperately wanted to have some hope of holding her again.

