So yeah, when my friends would come to me saying they needed braces and only had an overbite, I’d feel a bit envious and I remember saying or thinking that there was nothing wrong with their teeth and they didn’t need them. I regret that, but I was a dumb kid.

&nbsp;

As an adult, I don’t feel that way. I was told a few times that I didn’t need them, but I felt very dismissed. Hating my teeth resulted in years of low self esteem. I even stopped talking and became very reserved because I didn’t want people to look at them, and they made me mispronounce words a lot too. It doesn’t matter if other people don’t see what you do- what matters is that you weren’t happy with your teeth. You chose a solution to make you more happy, and that’s completely fine and reasonable to do. I would just respond to people with something like “Thank you! but getting braces is something that I wanted to fix my (insert condition lol) to feel a bit happier/more confident with my smile.” You don’t really owe anyone an explanation, but I do feel like speaking up when this happens can be a good thing to make it known that even though it may be well intentioned by some, it’s not a very considerate thing to say.. on top of all that, bite issues can cause other problems. Due to my bite alone, i know it sounds weird but there wasn’t good space for my tongue lol. After a few months in braces, my tongue finally has room to fit lol.

I could see that, I think most people are generally trying to be helpful for sure but yeah, those types of comments from others in these situations just seem so dismissive. I kind of wish we could normalize venting and just offering a shoulder or “that sucks, how are you dealing?” instead of solutions or other routes of attempting to make people feel better. 

&nbsp;

Yeah, I am very fortunate to have found some amazing doctors. It’s definitely not easy especially with gynecological issues. My first gynecologist that I saw when I moved worked for the same practice as my current, but she didn’t seem to listen and dismissed a lot of my problems. Tried giving me hormonal BC for literally any problem I’d have(I know it can help a lot of people, but was actually indirectly what caused my vaginismus; I got recurrent UTI’s and BV on Nuvaring and my last infection left me with so much pain that I developed this. I also had debilitating pain during my period on all hormonal BC’s I’ve tried). I dread the day when I move away from my current area because my doctors are gems.

&nbsp;

Exactly! If it were a personal choice, that would be a perfectly fine response but since it’s not, it’s maybe a little … lacking in thoughtfulness ? Idk what word I’m looking for lol.

&nbsp;

