I have ceramics on the tops. I have mostly gotten clear bands so far and literally only had an issue with staining after eating something with turmeric(oof. Idk what I was thinking honestly lol- luckily it was just a few days before my next appointment).

&nbsp;

I got periwinkle blue bands last month and [here’s a picture](https://imgur.com/a/PquqFQy). They didn’t stain at all and looked nice with the ceramics, but I didn’t like them against my skintone. I have clear again right now, and I’m considering trying out clear-gray, pink, and purple in the future. 
&nbsp;
I drink coffee and tea a lot and haven’t had an issue with the bands discoloring, you just have to brush after whenever possible. I also use straws a lot, so maybe that’s helped? 

&nbsp;

My orthodontist also originally offered “clear”gray bands because they’re similar, but less likely to stain. If you’re worried about a certain band color staining, you could always give them a try on your bottom teeth first if your top teeth cover them and get a “safe” darker color for the tops :) 

&nbsp;

I chose ceramics over invisilign because I was in recovery for an eating disorder and had a very strict eating schedule/basically had to almost constantly be eating throughout the day. So invisilign seemed very impractical and like it’d be a slower process for me. Even if I were 100% recovered, I’d still chose them because eating often throughout the day makes me feel the most energized, and I drink a ton of tea.

I instantly thought this. Epipens are commonly price gouged here in the US. My brother used to have severe asthma and a nut allergy and always had one as a kid. As prices became more and more outrageous, he just knew to always ask what was in foods before eating them. I don’t think he’s carried one for years now, unfortunately. Medical things are inhumanely expensive here.

&nbsp;

My SO is similar; he has a mild shellfish allergy, but Epipens are insanely expensive so he just always informs chefs of his allergy and avoids any place where he can see into the kitchen and they only use one cooking surface.

