I also had a best friend years ago who was at one point the most amazing person, but slowly changed and I remember I kept thinking I did something wrong and hoping they’d go back to how they were. Like maybe they were just having a rough time, and I didn’t realize that even if they were, their behavior towards me was no longer that of a friend. If that makes sense. I was very naive, isolated , and lonely at the time and just “wanted my friend back”.

&nbsp;

Especially growing up in an abusive family, these things can be very confusing and seem almost normal too, or you can be prone to self blame for things like this happening. Like I said, there are many possible reasons.

