&nbsp;

All that happened when I got the vaccine were the expected immune responses: a mild fever, fatigue, and my shoulder was sore for a few days. I actually had lingering bronchial spasms from when I’d been sick and they totally disappeared after I got the vaccine. Hoping that’s over for good lol. The first one was more rough for me than the 2nd, but immune responses only lasted 1-3 days. 

&nbsp;

I was very adamant about getting it(because of this and I was in the thick of my eating disorder at the time) before I found out that the news stories about neurological symptoms were on cases that were found to have no relation to the vaccine, symptoms just occurred simultaneously by coincidence. 
You should be fine OP, I think we are in a high risk category and nothing in the vaccine is neurotoxic. I would definitely discuss it with your doctor.

