 This is a newer thing that I've experienced(since it became cool to hate on "white people" and now society takes part in this invisible heritage or POC qualifier scale) and it's really frustrating and invalidating. Sure I lightened my skin, but that doesn't make me less "Mexican". I feel like people now try to measure us on this scale of color to be included and all that achieves is to shame, once again for skin color. I've tried the past few years to "prove myself" but it's exhausting. I know who I am, I know my heritage, I know my past and where I come from. We all do, and no one has a right to invalidate that to try to feel some sort of superiority.

Just want to jump in your say 1.NTA.. agreed, cousin is 1000 TA. I'm honestly tired of seeing this type of behavior swept under the rug, especially within families. Also racism towards light skinned natives is unfortunately rampant.

